    "why_wp43_failed": "WP43 treated a structural alert as a VETO. Permissive used PAINS only, which misses two of the three BRENK-only frequent hitters; strict rejected on ANY BRENK alert, which flags aspirin's phenol_ester. Both are binary uses of a signal that does not carry binary information.",
    "what_changed": "A graded alert-count penalty was tried first and ALSO failed, for a reason that is a result in itself: every control clears every hard gate, so alert count is the only separating feature, and the panel is non-monotone (metformin must pass with 2 alerts; nitrogen mustard must fail with 1). Exhaustive enumeration of every 'n_alerts <= k' rule caps that family at balanced accuracy 0.7. The rule was therefore changed in KIND, not in threshold: only a REACTIVE (non-specific electrophile) alert rejects; a structural/metabolic alert is carried as a flag. The authoring-panel result (1.0) is a demonstration, not evidence - the mechanistic mapping was written with that panel in view. The hold-out panel result (0.75) is the only evidence."
  },
  "experimental_plan": {
    "P11_experimental_success_rate": {
      "question": "what fraction of designs work?",
      "why_unmeasurable_here": "n = 0 designs have been synthesised, so the rate has no denominator",
      "resolution": "the only resolution is to make the designs and count",
      "design": {
        "entities": [
